I found no bugs; both findings are test-coverage gaps, at consider severity. Nothing was run; I read the code only. The logic checks out against the call sites. The cached listing is cleared after an AO boot finishes, `ownBoots` is cleared by the deferred function in `Boot`, and `restartHub` falls back to `reviveHub` if the hub fails to start. The test assertions match what the code does. The gaps: `restartHub` and the `recordBoots` call inside `EnsureReady` are never run under test, because every test swaps in a fake `replaceHub`. The tests that cover recording boots skip off macOS, because `unlistedSimulators` returns early on any other OS.

